    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Shanaya,</div><div><br></div><div>Jupyter notebooks are free for anyone to use. You can install them by installing miniconda (<a href=\"https://docs.conda.io/en/latest/miniconda.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://docs.conda.io/en/latest/miniconda.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465857992000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2RR1IoTfnG-jBwnDw5bhDW\">https://docs.conda.io/en/latest/miniconda.html</a>). <br></div><div>After downloading the right script for your computer, run the following commands in bash/terminal:</div><div><br></div><div><div><pre><span>bash Miniconda*.sh</span><span></span></pre></div></div><div><br></div><div>and follow the steps.</div><div><br></div><div>Then run <br></div><div><pre><span>conda</span> <span>config</span> <span>--</span><span>add</span> <span>channels</span> <span>conda-forge<br>conda install jupyter notebook<br>jupyter notebook<br></span></pre></div><div><br></div><div>A jupyter notebook should open in your browser. <br></div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Taylor<br> </div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Tue, May 14, 2019 at 1:36 PM Shanaya Shah &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">shs...@ucdavis.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
